  "interpretation": "Frames are captured while the source keeps presenting. identical_to_previous means the desktop had not changed between captures; unique_frames versus captured_frames therefore bounds the observable output rate. expected_step_ms tracks the ground-truth time between unique frames; negative steps (backward_steps) mean a later capture showed an earlier moment. source_phase_ms is the matched instant's distance from the nearest real source frame instant: a real frame (captured, held, or re-presented) sits within real_frame_phase_tolerance_ms of zero, a generated frame does not, and a session that never generated a frame scores every unique frame as real however good its PSNR looks. Pixel metrics are best-aligned image variance and do not prove monitor presentation."
